---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MemoryLab from '../../components/MemoryLab.astro';
import VideoDemo from '../../components/VideoDemo.astro';
import '../../styles/memory-lab.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Memory Lab | David Blumenau" description="Explore a real historical sample from PanelForge's knowledge graph. Follow a connection, inspect its meaning and try a reversible local edit.">
  <main id="main" class="memory-page">
    <section class="ml-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="ml-back" href="/work/knowledge-graph/"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> The knowledge graph story</a><div class="ml-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Memory Lab / An interactive field guide</p><h1>A fact is a<br /><em>starting point.</em></h1></div><div class="ml-hero-copy"><p>A graph makes a connection visible. Its names, sources and corrections make that connection worth trusting.</p><p>Explore a small part of my actual project graph, then practice a correction you can undo.</p><span class="ml-sample-notice">A real project-data sample. Edits here stay in this browser.</span></div></div><div class="ml-hero-foot"><span>31 original entity labels / 33 distinct connections</span><span>Historical extraction sample · checked 14 October 2026</span></div></section>
    <div class="wrap"><MemoryLab /></div>
    <section class="ml-context wrap" aria-labelledby="ml-context-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">The reading rules</p><h2 id="ml-context-title">Memory needs<br /><em>a little doubt.</em></h2></div><div class="ml-context-notes"><article><span>01</span><h3>A name is not a verdict.</h3><p><code>vue</code>, <code>vue-js</code> and <code>vue-3</code> appear as separate labels in this sample. They may overlap in meaning. That alone is not enough evidence to merge them, and a versioned name may carry useful context.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>A line is a claim to inspect.</h3><p><code>built_with</code> is the graph's stored predicate. Read it in its source context: a conversation might concern one component, prototype or stage of the project. This sample is not a map of today's architecture.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>A correction needs a return path.</h3><p>The lab preserves the selected tuple and previous view for undo. The real curation work uses action records and before-state snapshots; this local illustration shows why a correction should remain inspectable.</p><a href="/features/graph-curation/" class="text-link">Read the curation story <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></article></div></section>
    <section class="ml-product wrap" aria-labelledby="ml-product-title"><div class="ml-product-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Behind the illustration</p><h2 id="ml-product-title">The graph I actually use.</h2><p>The interactive lab gives the data a small, readable stage. This recording shows the real PanelForge graph: searching for the project, filtering build relationships and focusing its neighborhood.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/knowledge-graph/">Read the full case study <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></div><VideoDemo src="/media/knowledge-graph-workflow.mp4" poster="/media/knowledge-graph.webp" title="Find PanelForge in the real graph" description="Search narrows the actual graph to PanelForge. A predicate filter selects build relationships, then selecting the project brings nearby software into focus. Zoom and fit change the view. Cuts shorten stationary pauses." captions="/media/knowledge-graph-workflow.vtt" mediaCaption="Actual product recording. The lab above uses a separately audited subset of the same filtered graph." /></section>
    <aside class="ml-sample-boundary wrap"><p class="eyebrow">What this sample contains</p><p>Thirty-three distinct subject / predicate / object tuples, drawn from 155 matching extracted records. Repeated identical tuples are shown once. Original software labels and types are retained, including two unknown types. The sample contains project and software names only. Edits last until this page is reloaded; they are not saved to the product.</p><a href="/features/" class="text-link">Explore the feature atlas <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></aside>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
